# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with the default core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# every text file to CRLF on checkout. helm itself tolerates that, but any gate
# that compares rendered output byte for byte starts failing for a reason nobody
# can see in a diff, and the same chart then renders differently on two
# machines. The chart is the deployment artifact, so it has to be identical
# everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The gate scripts are run directly and must keep LF: a CRLF shebang line makes
# the kernel look for an interpreter whose name ends in a carriage return.
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
